From 0b94f1de29cabb29bc166b2662d089b9db939ca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:00:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Footprint area of the visibility bound: projected ellipse
 (--sem_contrib_area)

- utils/projected_area.py recomputes the 2D covariance of the visible Gaussians with
  the rasterizer's formulas (computeCov2D, +0.3 low-pass) and returns the area of the
  projected 3-sigma ellipse, 9 pi sqrt(det). The smallest rectangle covering the ellipse
  has area 36 sqrt(det), i.e. the same quantity times 4 / pi.
- --sem_contrib_area ellipse|disc (default ellipse) selects the footprint used by
  --sem_min_contrib_px. A disc of the long-axis radius penalises elongated Gaussians.
- Logging: contribution / ellipse area is accumulated next to the disc version
  (sem_log: contrib_px_ellipse_*, snapshots: contrib_per_px_ellipse).
- A one-time message compares the recomputed long-axis radius with the rasterizer's radii.
- run_decisive.sh: CONTRIB_AREA environment variable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PHmjveU9kNqt1TKBUX99W4
